IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part IV, "Objection and Review": sections 103 to 105.
-- The appeal to the Tax Court of Canada (time, extension, what the Court may do), the authority to decide questions, the
-- finality of decisions and rulings, the allowance for a person who attends, and the finality of the Court's decision.
-- Written by piece ei3 (Sonnet 5.5). LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Unofficial plain-text source; nothing verified
-- against the official text.
--
-- OUT OF RANGE, taken as inputs: section 167 of the Income Tax Act (not deposited); the rule made under paragraph 20(1.1)(h.1)
-- of the Tax Court of Canada Act (not deposited); the Federal Courts Act (not deposited).
-- Time limits: "within 90 days after the decision is communicated" ends on that day PLUS 90 and that day counts (keel fork F4).

§ `Section 103 - appeal to the Tax Court of Canada`

-- Subsection (1): the Commission or a person affected by a decision on an appeal to the Minister under s 91 or 92 may appeal "within 90
-- days after the decision is communicated ..., or within such longer time as the Court allows on application made to it within 90
-- days after the expiration of those 90 days". Two stages: day 90 (the last day of 90 days after communication) and day 180 (90
-- days after day 90). The Court's decision to allow a longer time, and the last day it allows, are inputs.
-- src:1711 | 103 (1) The Commission or a person affected by a decision on an appeal to the Minister under section 91 or 92 may appeal from the decision to the Tax Court of Canada in accordance with the Tax Court of Canada Act and the applicable rules of court made thereunder within 90 days after the decision is communicated to the Commission or the person, or within such longer time as the Court allows on application made to it within 90 days after the expiration of those 90 days.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 103(1) (src:1711)
GIVEN `the day on which the decision is communicated to the Commission or the person` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the application to the Court for a longer time was made, if one was` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 103(1) the application for a longer time was made in time` IS
    CONSIDER `the day on which the application to the Court for a longer time was made, if one was`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST appliedOn THEN
        appliedOn AT MOST (`the last day of` 90 `days after` (`the last day of` 90 `days after` `the day on which the decision is communicated to the Commission or the person`))

-- src:1711 | 103 (1) The Commission or a person affected by a decision on an appeal to the Minister under section 91 or 92 may appeal from the decision to the Tax Court of Canada in accordance with the Tax Court of Canada Act and the applicable rules of court made thereunder within 90 days after the decision is communicated to the Commission or the person, or within such longer time as the Court allows on application made to it within 90 days after the expiration of those 90 days.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 103(1) (src:1711)
GIVEN `the day on which the appeal is brought` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the longer time the Court allowed, if it allowed one` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 103(1) the appeal is brought within the longer time the Court allowed` IS
    CONSIDER `the last day of the longer time the Court allowed, if it allowed one`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST allowedUntil THEN `the day on which the appeal is brought` AT MOST allowedUntil

-- src:1711 | 103 (1) The Commission or a person affected by a decision on an appeal to the Minister under section 91 or 92 may appeal from the decision to the Tax Court of Canada in accordance with the Tax Court of Canada Act and the applicable rules of court made thereunder within 90 days after the decision is communicated to the Commission or the person, or within such longer time as the Court allows on application made to it within 90 days after the expiration of those 90 days.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 103(1) (src:1711)
GIVEN `the appellant is the Commission or a person affected by a decision on an appeal to the Minister under section 91 or 92` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the decision is communicated to the Commission or the person` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the appeal is brought` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the application to the Court for a longer time was made, if one was` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the last day of the longer time the Court allowed, if it allowed one` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 103(1) the appeal to the Tax Court of Canada is brought in time` IF
        `the appellant is the Commission or a person affected by a decision on an appeal to the Minister under section 91 or 92`
    AND (    `the day on which the appeal is brought` AT MOST (`the last day of` 90 `days after` `the day on which the decision is communicated to the Commission or the person`)
         OR  (    `s 103(1) the application for a longer time was made in time` `the day on which the decision is communicated to the Commission or the person` `the day on which the application to the Court for a longer time was made, if one was`
              AND `s 103(1) the appeal is brought within the longer time the Court allowed` `the day on which the appeal is brought` `the last day of the longer time the Court allowed, if it allowed one`))

-- src:1713 | (1.1) Section 167, except paragraph 167(5)(a), of the Income Tax Act applies, with such modifications as the circumstances require, in respect of applications made under subsection (1).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 103(1.1) (src:1713)
GIVEN `the application is made under subsection 103(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 103(1.1) section 167 of the Income Tax Act, except paragraph 167(5)(a), applies to the application` IF
    `the application is made under subsection 103(1)`

-- Subsection (2): the time at which a decision is communicated is determined by the rule, if any, made under paragraph
-- 20(1.1)(h.1) of the Tax Court of Canada Act (not deposited). With no such rule the section gives no time (NOTHING).
-- src:1715 | (2) The determination of the time at which a decision on an appeal to the Minister under section 91 or 92 is communicated to the Commission or to a person shall be made in accordance with the rule, if any, made under paragraph 20(1.1)(h.1) of the Tax Court of Canada Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 103(2) (src:1715)
GIVEN `the time determined in accordance with the rule, if any, made under paragraph 20(1.1)(h.1) of the Tax Court of Canada Act` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `s 103(2) the day on which a decision on an appeal to the Minister is communicated` IS
    `the time determined in accordance with the rule, if any, made under paragraph 20(1.1)(h.1) of the Tax Court of Canada Act`

-- Subsection (3): on an appeal the Tax Court of Canada (a) may vacate, confirm or vary a decision on an appeal under s 91 or an
-- assessment appealed under s 92; (b) on an appeal under s 92, may refer the matter back to the Minister for reconsideration and
-- reassessment; (c) shall notify the parties in writing; (d) shall give reasons, which need not be in writing unless the Court
-- deems it advisable in a particular case.
-- src:1717 | (3) On an appeal, the Tax Court of Canada
-- src:1718 | (a) may vacate, confirm or vary a decision on an appeal under section 91 or an assessment that is the subject of an appeal under section 92;
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 103(3)(a) (src:1717-1718)
GIVEN `the appeal concerns a decision on an appeal under section 91 or an assessment that is the subject of an appeal under section 92` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 103(3)(a) the Court may vacate, confirm or vary the decision or the assessment` IF
    `the appeal concerns a decision on an appeal under section 91 or an assessment that is the subject of an appeal under section 92`

-- src:1717 | (3) On an appeal, the Tax Court of Canada
-- src:1718 | (a) may vacate, confirm or vary a decision on an appeal under section 91 or an assessment that is the subject of an appeal under section 92;
-- src:1719 | (b) in the case of an appeal under section 92, may refer the matter back to the Minister for reconsideration and reassessment;
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 103(3)(b) (src:1717) (src:1719)
GIVEN `the appeal is an appeal under section 92` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 103(3)(b) the Court may refer the matter back to the Minister for reconsideration and reassessment` IF
    `the appeal is an appeal under section 92`

-- src:1717 | (3) On an appeal, the Tax Court of Canada
-- src:1718 | (a) may vacate, confirm or vary a decision on an appeal under section 91 or an assessment that is the subject of an appeal under section 92;
-- src:1719 | (b) in the case of an appeal under section 92, may refer the matter back to the Minister for reconsideration and reassessment;
-- src:1720 | (c) shall notify in writing the parties to the appeal of its decision; and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 103(3)(c) (src:1717) (src:1720)
GIVEN `there is an appeal to the Tax Court of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 103(3)(c) the Court shall notify in writing the parties to the appeal of its decision` IF
    `there is an appeal to the Tax Court of Canada`

-- src:1717 | (3) On an appeal, the Tax Court of Canada
-- src:1718 | (a) may vacate, confirm or vary a decision on an appeal under section 91 or an assessment that is the subject of an appeal under section 92;
-- src:1719 | (b) in the case of an appeal under section 92, may refer the matter back to the Minister for reconsideration and reassessment;
-- src:1720 | (c) shall notify in writing the parties to the appeal of its decision; and
-- src:1721 | (d) give reasons for its decision but, except where the Court deems it advisable in a particular case to give reasons in writing, the reasons given by it need not be in writing.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 103(3)(d) (src:1717) (src:1721)
GIVEN `the Court deems it advisable in the particular case to give reasons in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 103(3)(d) the Court's reasons must be given in writing` IF
    `the Court deems it advisable in the particular case to give reasons in writing`

§ `Sections 104 and 105 - authority, finality, allowances`

-- Subsection (1): "any question of fact or law necessary to be decided in the course of an appeal under section 91 or 103 or to
-- reconsider an assessment under section 92", and whether a person may be or is affected by the decision or assessment.
-- src:1723 | 104 (1) The Tax Court of Canada and the Minister have authority to decide any question of fact or law necessary to be decided in the course of an appeal under section 91 or 103 or to reconsider an assessment under section 92 and to decide whether a person may be or is affected by the decision or assessment.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 104(1) (src:1723)
GIVEN `the question is a question of fact or law necessary to be decided in the course of an appeal under section 91 or 103 or to reconsider an assessment under section 92` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the question is whether a person may be or is affected by the decision or assessment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 104(1) the Tax Court of Canada and the Minister have authority to decide the question` IF
        `the question is a question of fact or law necessary to be decided in the course of an appeal under section 91 or 103 or to reconsider an assessment under section 92`
    OR  `the question is whether a person may be or is affected by the decision or assessment`

-- Subsection (2): "Except as otherwise provided in this Act", a decision of the Tax Court of Canada or the Minister and a ruling of
-- an authorized officer under s 90 are final and binding for all purposes of the Act.
-- src:1725 | (2) Except as otherwise provided in this Act, a decision of the Tax Court of Canada or the Minister and a ruling of an authorized officer under section 90 are final and binding for all purposes of this Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 104(2) (src:1725)
GIVEN `it is a decision of the Tax Court of Canada or the Minister, or a ruling of an authorized officer under section 90` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this Act otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 104(2) the decision or ruling is final and binding for all purposes of this Act` IF
        `it is a decision of the Tax Court of Canada or the Minister, or a ruling of an authorized officer under section 90`
    AND (NOT `this Act otherwise provides`)

-- Subsection (3): a person affected by the Minister's decision, who is requested by the Court to attend on the consideration of the
-- appeal and attends, "shall be paid such travel and other allowances, including compensation for loss of remunerative time, as are
-- approved by the Treasury Board". The amount is the Treasury Board's approval (an input).
-- src:1727 | (3) If, on an appeal to the Tax Court of Canada from a decision of the Minister, a person affected by the decision is requested by the Court to attend before it on the consideration of the appeal and so attends, the person shall be paid such travel and other allowances, including compensation for loss of remunerative time, as are approved by the Treasury Board.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 104(3) (src:1727)
GIVEN `the appeal is to the Tax Court of Canada from a decision of the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a person affected by the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court requested the person to attend before it on the consideration of the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person attends` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 104(3) the person shall be paid travel and other allowances approved by the Treasury Board` IF
        `the appeal is to the Tax Court of Canada from a decision of the Minister`
    AND `the person is a person affected by the decision`
    AND `the Court requested the person to attend before it on the consideration of the appeal`
    AND `the person attends`

-- src:1727 | (3) If, on an appeal to the Tax Court of Canada from a decision of the Minister, a person affected by the decision is requested by the Court to attend before it on the consideration of the appeal and so attends, the person shall be paid such travel and other allowances, including compensation for loss of remunerative time, as are approved by the Treasury Board.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 104(3) (src:1727)
GIVEN `the person shall be paid allowances under subsection 104(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount approved by the Treasury Board for travel and other allowances, including compensation for loss of remunerative time` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 104(3) the allowances payable` IS
    IF `the person shall be paid allowances under subsection 104(3)`
    THEN JUST `the amount approved by the Treasury Board for travel and other allowances, including compensation for loss of remunerative time`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Section 105: the Court's decision under s 103 is final and, "except for an appeal under the Federal Courts Act", not subject to
-- appeal to or review by any court. An appeal under the Federal Courts Act is outside this section (NOTHING); any other appeal or
-- review of a s 103 decision: JUST FALSE. Anything that is not a s 103 decision: NOTHING.
-- src:1729 | 105 The decision of the Tax Court of Canada under section 103 is final and, except for an appeal under the Federal Courts Act, is not subject to appeal to or review by any court.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 105 (src:1729)
GIVEN `it is a decision of the Tax Court of Canada under section 103` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeding is an appeal under the Federal Courts Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 105 the decision is subject to appeal to or review by a court` IS
    IF `it is a decision of the Tax Court of Canada under section 103` AND (NOT `the proceeding is an appeal under the Federal Courts Act`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING
